? Which projection has parallel projectors perpendicular to the view plane?
+ Orthographic
- Perspective
- Oblique
- Spherical panorama
= Orthographic is the perpendicular parallel case.

? In perspective with COP origin and plane z = d, what is x′?
+ xd/z
- xz/d
- x+d
- x−z
= Similar triangles give x′/x = d/z.

? Project (5,4,7) perspectively onto z = 5. What is x′?
+ 25/7
- 7
- 1
- 35
= x′ = 5×5/7.

? What happens to equal-size objects at greater depth in perspective?
+ They generally appear smaller
- They must remain equal size
- They necessarily become wider
- Their projected size doubles
= This is perspective foreshortening.

? What does a vanishing point represent?
+ Image convergence of a parallel direction
- The physical camera centre itself
- The nearest model control vertex
- The origin of every world system
= A vanishing point is not the COP.

? What is cabinet projection’s receding-depth scale?
+ Half scale
- Full scale
- Double scale
- Zero scale
= Cabinet halves the receding perpendicular-to-XY lengths.

? Translate P(2,3,1) by T(2,1,4). What results?
+ (4,4,5)
- (4,3,4)
- (0,2,−3)
- (2,1,4)
= Add each shift to its matching coordinate.

? Which coordinate remains fixed in origin-centred X-axis rotation?
+ x
- y
- z
- All coordinates
= The YZ pair rotates while x stays fixed.

? Which homogeneous point represents Cartesian (2,3,4) with h = 1?
+ (2,3,4,1)
- (1,2,3,4)
- (2,3,4,0)
- (2,3,1,4)
= Append the homogeneous coordinate 1.

? What does a wireframe primarily show?
+ Geometric edges or curves
- Only the final surface colour
- Only recorded stereo audio
- Only the camera file name
= Wireframes reveal structure.

? How can moving control vertices affect an object?
+ Its local curve or surface shape
- Only the monitor resolution
- Only the source file extension
- Only the physical screen size
= Control vertices influence the geometry.

? What does head tracking contribute to a CAVE?
+ Viewpoint-dependent perspective updates
- Permanent orthographic-only images
- Automatic removal of all stereo views
- A fixed image regardless of movement
= The rendered view changes with the tracked viewer.
